    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35353" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">perpessīcĭus</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-tĭus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		perpetior, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>that can endure much</i>, <i>that has
				endured much</i>, <i>patient</i>, <i>enduring</i> (postAug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">etiam a duro et perpessicio confessionem
					accipit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 53, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Socrates perpessicius senex,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 104, 27</span></i>
			.</div>
